    "result_text": "The build is green. Let me verify the observable contract end-to-end by checking the audit log output already captured and confirming the region stays plain while identifiers changed.\n\nThe test passed and the audit output confirms the behavior:\n- `memberId=NSW27730A26006` \u2014 region prefix stays plain **NSW** (so `locality`/`timezone`/segment stay plain), while the hash portion now mixes in the `V2` tag.\n- Audit event now carries `\"segment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\"` and `\"schemaVersion\":2`.\n\n## Summary\n\nReleased version 2 of the owner identity while keeping structural impact low \u2014 each change is a one-line edit inside a small, cohesive class, plus one tiny new class.\n\n**Version-2 identifier derivation** (the `V2` tag mixed in, so every identifier changes and no v1 value recurs):\n- New `IdentityRegion.v2(owner)` (`service/IdentityRegion.java`) \u2014 the single \"region code used inside the identifiers\": the plain region with a fixed `\"V2|\"` tag mixed in.\n- `MemberId.generate` \u2014 feeds `IdentityRegion.v2` into the HASH8 input (visible region prefix stays plain, so extraction is unaffected).\n- `HouseholdMatcher.householdId` \u2014 prefixes the household key with the v2 region.\n- `IdentityKey.of` \u2014 prefixes the key input with the v2 region.\n\nBecause the memberId's visible region *prefix* is left plain, `RegionCode.of` still returns e.g. `NSW`, so `locality`, `timezone` and the owner segment's derived region keep the plain code \u2014 the `V2` tag lives only inside the hashed identifiers.\n\n**Response shape** (`openapi.yml` + `OwnerMapper`):\n- New `OwnerIdentity` schema grouping `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`; those three removed from top-level `Owner`.\n- Added top-level integer `apiVersion` of `2`.\n- Mapper maps `apiVersion` to `2` and builds the nested `identity` object via a small `toIdentity` default method.\n\n**Audit schema v2** (`OwnerCreatedEvent.emit`):\n- Added `\"schemaVersion\":2` and a `\"segment\"` recomputed from the v2 identity.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged. `./mvnw test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.",
