    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered enumeration for `POST /api/owners`. I've split it into what happens *before* anything is persisted (validations) and what mutates state (side-effects), all in execution order.\n\n## Phase 0 \u2014 Request routing & authorization\n1. **Authorization gate**: `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 caller must be an owner-admin (403 otherwise).\n2. **Route disambiguation**: if an `Idempotency-Key` header is present, `IdempotentOwnerController` handles it (in-memory `ConcurrentHashMap` replay cache); otherwise `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` handles it directly. The idempotent path delegates to the same method, so all logic below is identical.\n\n## Phase 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on the request body (`OwnerFieldsDto`)\nFires before the controller body runs; failures \u2192 400 via `MethodArgumentNotValidException`.\n\n3. `firstName` \u2014 **@NotNull**, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$`\n4. `lastName` \u2014 **@NotNull**, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` `^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$`\n5. `city` \u2014 **@NotNull**, `@Size(1..80)`, `@Pattern` `.*\\S.*` (non-blank)\n6. `telephone` \u2014 **@NotNull**, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern` `^[+()\\d\\s-]+$`\n7. `title` \u2014 `@Size(1..10)` (optional)\n8. `address`, `addressLine1`, `addressLine2` \u2014 each `@Size(1..255)` + `@Pattern` `.*\\S.*` (optional)\n9. `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` + `@Email` (optional)\n10. `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern` `^\\d{4}$` (optional)\n11. `registrationDate`, `birthDate` \u2014 `@Valid` date binding (optional)\n- *(`sharesHousehold` \u2014 no constraints; read separately, never mapped onto the entity)*\n\n## Phase 2 \u2014 Mapper-level validation + normalization (`OwnerMapper.toOwner`)\nRuns next; any throw here \u2192 400 via the `IllegalArgumentException` handler. These are **both validations and transforming side-effects** on the in-memory entity:\n\n12. **Telephone normalization** (`normalizeTelephone`): strips non-digits, prepends `61` for local numbers (dropping a leading `0`), validates the result is 8\u201315 digits, then `E164NationalLength.check` (exactly 9 national digits for `+61`, 10 for `+1`). Produces `+<digits>`.\n13. **Address composition** (`composeAddress`/`normalizeLine` \u2192 `AddressNormalizer`): prefers `addressLine1(+2)` over flat `address`; trims, collapses whitespace, upper-cases, expands `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`; **throws if blank** after normalization.\n14. **Postcode validation** (`PostcodeValidator.validate` via `LocalityResolver`): if a postcode is supplied, it must fall in the city's region range (NSW 2000\u20132099 / VIC 3000\u20133099 / QLD 4000\u20134099); else throws.\n15. **Registration date validation** (`RegistrationDateValidator.validate`): rejects a future date (null allowed).\n16. **Disposable email rejection** (`DisposableEmailDomain.validate`): throws if domain \u2208 {mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}.\n17. **Salutation composition** (`composeSalutation`): sets `salutation` = `title + \" \" + lastName` (or just `lastName`).\n18. Entity setters mutate on assignment: `setEmail` lower-cases the email; `setRegistrationDate` defaults null\u2192today then rolls the date forward off weekends/holidays via `BusinessDay.adjust`.\n\n## Phase 3 \u2014 Business-rule guards (controller)\nAll owners are loaded (`findAllOwners`), then three guards throw `RejectedRequestException` (rendered as RFC-7807):\n\n19. **Daily registration limit** (`DailyRegistrationLimit.isReached`): \u2265 100 owners registered today \u2192 **429**.\n20. **Duplicate identity** (`IdentityKey.isDuplicate`): SHA-256 of `region|telephone|lowerEmail|Soundex(lastName)` collides with an existing non-deleted owner \u2192 **409**.\n21. **City capacity** (`CityCapacity.isFull`): \u2265 50 owners in the same city (case-insensitive) \u2192 **409**.\n\n## Phase 4 \u2014 Enrichment side-effects (`OwnerRegistration.enrich`, before save)\nSets derived fields on the entity (most are `@Transient`):\n\n22. `namesakeCount` \u2014 count of case-insensitive first+last name matches.\n23. `memberId` \u2014 generated `<REGION><FY2><HASH8><Luhn>`, de-duplicated against existing member IDs.\n24. `bulkSignupWarning` \u2014 true if > 80 owners registered today.\n25. `capacityWarning` \u2014 true if city has 40\u201349 owners (approaching full).\n26. `householdSize` \u2014 computed from household matching.\n27. `possibleDuplicateOf` \u2014 soft-duplicate match (postcode + lastName soundex), unless `sharesHousehold` is true.\n28. `membershipLevel` \u2014 capped at max household level + 1.\n\n## Phase 5 \u2014 Persistence\n29. **Save** (`ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`, `@Transactional`): `ownerRepository.save(owner)` via the Spring Data JPA repository. Entity-level `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern` constraints on `Owner`/`Person` (firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone `^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$`) are checked by Hibernate at persist. ID assigned via `@GeneratedValue(IDENTITY)`.\n- *(No `@PrePersist`/entity listeners exist.)*\n\n## Phase 6 \u2014 Post-save side-effects (`OwnerCreatedEvent.emit`)\n30. **Audit log** \u2014 human-readable `AUDIT` line (id, memberId, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n31. **Structured audit log** \u2014 JSON `OWNER_CREATED` line with a monotonic sequence number and schema version 2.\n32. **Welcome notification** (`WelcomeNotification.enqueue`) \u2014 emits a `NOTIFY` log line (the \"welcome email\").\n- *(These are logger emissions, not Spring `ApplicationEvent`s \u2014 invoked synchronously inline. No `@EventListener`/`@TransactionalEventListener` fire.)*\n33. **Idempotency cache write** (only on the idempotent path): the resulting `OwnerDto` is stored under the `Idempotency-Key`.\n\n## Phase 7 \u2014 Response\n34. Map to `OwnerDto` (computes derived read-only fields: displayName, initials, membership points/level, segment, etc.), set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header, return **201 Created**.\n\n---\n\n**Two important caveats to note:**\n- The `sharesHousehold` request field is used only to influence `possibleDuplicateOf` enrichment (step 27) \u2014 it is *never* stored on the entity.\n- The `CallMonitoringAspect` does **not** apply here: under the active `spring-data-jpa` profile the repository proxy isn't `@Repository`-annotated, so its pointcut doesn't match. No servlet filters or interceptors exist beyond the Spring Security chain."
